### Current Behavior

Installing `@nx/storybook` always installs `@nx/cypress` because it is listed under `dependencies` (not an optional peer). Workspaces that use Storybook with Playwright/Vitest and never use Cypress still get `@nx/cypress` in the install graph.

The only runtime `require('@nx/cypress/...')` in the package is the optional preset `@nx/storybook/presets/cypress` (`nxE2EStorybookPreset`), a thin wrapper around `nxE2EPreset` that sets `baseUrl` to Storybook’s default port. Storybook executors/plugin/configuration generator do not need `@nx/cypress` at runtime. A leftover `configureCypress: true` default remains in schema normalization but is no longer a schema option.

Confirmed on `@nx/storybook@22.7.1` and still present on `@nx/storybook@23.2.1`.

### Expected Behavior

`@nx/cypress` should be an **optional peerDependency** (or live in a separate optional package), so it is only installed when consumers use `@nx/storybook/presets/cypress` / Cypress e2e against Storybook — consistent with `@nx/web`, where `@nx/cypress` is already an optional peer.

### GitHub Repo

N/A — reproducible from published package metadata:

```bash
npm view @nx/storybook@23.2.1 dependencies.@nx/cypress
# => 23.2.1
```

### Steps to Reproduce

1. `pnpm add -D @nx/storybook@23.2.1` (or any recent 22/23) in a workspace that does **not** depend on Cypress.
2. `pnpm why @nx/cypress` → pulled by `@nx/storybook`.
3. Inspect `@nx/storybook/presets/cypress.js` → sole `require('@nx/cypress/...')`.

