## Goal

A system tray icon that shows runtime status at a glance and gives quick access
to the dashboard and runtime controls.

Depends on: #3 (Tauri commands must be wired up first).

---

## Behaviour

| State | Icon | Menu items |
|---|---|---|
| Runtime reachable (Linux: pelagos in PATH; macOS: VM running) | solid icon | Open Dashboard, ── , Quit |
| Runtime unreachable | dimmed/greyed icon | Open Dashboard, Start VM (macOS only), ──, Quit |

The icon itself is the only persistent status indicator.  No tooltip text required for v0.1.

---

## Implementation in `src-tauri/src/lib.rs`

```rust
use tauri::{
    menu::{Menu, MenuItem, PredefinedMenuItem},
    tray::{MouseButton, MouseButtonState, TrayIconBuilder, TrayIconEvent},
    Manager,
};

pub fn run() {
    env_logger::init();

    // ... backend init (from issue #3) ...

    tauri::Builder::default()
        .manage(backend)
        .invoke_handler(tauri::generate_handler![...])
        .setup(|app| {
            // Build tray menu.
            let open   = MenuItem::with_id(app, "open",   "Open Dashboard", true, None::<&str>)?;
            let sep    = PredefinedMenuItem::separator(app)?;
            let quit   = MenuItem::with_id(app, "quit",   "Quit", true, None::<&str>)?;
            let menu   = Menu::with_items(app, &[&open, &sep, &quit])?;

            TrayIconBuilder::new()
                .icon(app.default_window_icon().unwrap().clone())
                .menu(&menu)
                .on_menu_event(|app, event| match event.id.as_ref() {
                    "open" => {
                        if let Some(win) = app.get_webview_window("main") {
                            let _ = win.show();
                            let _ = win.set_focus();
                        }
                    }
                    "quit" => app.exit(0),
                    _ => {}
                })
                .on_tray_icon_event(|tray, event| {
                    // Left-click opens dashboard (macOS/Linux convenience).
                    if let TrayIconEvent::Click {
                        button: MouseButton::Left,
                        button_state: MouseButtonState::Up,
                        ..
                    } = event
                    {
                        let app = tray.app_handle();
                        if let Some(win) = app.get_webview_window("main") {
                            let _ = win.show();
                            let _ = win.set_focus();
                        }
                    }
                })
                .build(app)?;

            // Hide the main window from the taskbar on Linux (show only via tray).
            if let Some(win) = app.get_webview_window("main") {
                // Window starts hidden per tauri.conf.json (visible: false).
                // Nothing to do here on startup.
                let _ = win; // suppress unused warning
            }

            Ok(())
        })
        .run(tauri::generate_context!())
        .expect("error while running tauri application");
}
```

