## Linux systray prerequisites

On Linux, Tauri uses `libayatana-appindicator3` for the system tray.
Create `scripts/install-dev-deps.sh`:

```bash
#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -euo pipefail
# Install system dependencies for pelagos-ui development on Linux.

if command -v pacman &>/dev/null; then
    sudo pacman -S --needed webkit2gtk-4.1 gtk3 libayatana-appindicator
elif command -v apt &>/dev/null; then
    sudo apt install -y libwebkit2gtk-4.1-dev libgtk-3-dev libayatana-appindicator3-dev
else
    echo "Unknown package manager — install webkit2gtk, gtk3, and libayatana-appindicator3 manually"
fi
```

Add the Tauri `tauri.conf.json` bundle config for Linux:
```json
"linux": {
  "deb": { "depends": ["libayatana-appindicator3-1"] },
  "appimage": { "bundleMediaFramework": true }
}
```

